---
source: tests/human_output.rs
description: "Created host, its enrollment command, and the default-role firewall note."
---
$ dn host create web-2 --network network-EXAMPLE
Created host "web-2" (host-Z3HWQ5ATVK2MRXE7NC4YLBPJDG)
  IP addresses: 100.100.0.40

To enroll the device, install dnclient and run:
  dnclient enroll EXAMPLE-ENROLLMENT-CODE

Note: the default role denies all inbound traffic. New hosts will be on
the network but unable to reach each other until a role with firewall
rules is created and assigned (see `dn role list`), unless one of their
tags carries firewall rules (see `dn tag get`).
